    "ADO-VALUES",
    "ADO-BATCH"
  ],
  "description": "ADO-VALUES on a client static batch-optimistic Recordset of SELECT ID, V, S FROM W ORDER BY ID (read/write copy), field V of row 1: set 100 and Update (cache) and UpdateBatch; set 120, Update and read Value, OriginalValue, UnderlyingValue and Status; a second Connection of the process sets V = 110; the three values; UpdateBatch (Errors); the values and Status; CancelBatch and the values; Resync(adAffectAll, adResyncUnderlyingValues) and the values; set 130, Update, UpdateBatch (Errors, values); then the stored row. Asks how the client cache separates original, staged and source values and whether the stale batch is refused.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
